        "original_id": "6221141c-3900-515c-a919-b729f141d19f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Newark, Nottinghamshire, England\n- Organizations: UK Parliament, House of Commons, Conservative Party, Labour Party, Standards Committee\n- People: Robert Jenrick, Patrick Mercer, Fiona Jones\n- Events: 1997 general election, 2001 general election, Newark by-election 2014, Patrick Mercer’s resignation\n\nFacts:\n- Fiona Jones was elected MP for Newark in Labour’s landslide victory in the 1997 general election.\n- Patrick Mercer was elected MP for Newark as a Conservative in the 2001 general election.\n- Patrick Mercer resigned the Conservative parliamentary whip in May 2013 following questions about paid advocacy.\n- Patrick Mercer served as an Independent MP for Newark until resigning at the end of April 2014 after the Standards Committee suspended him for six months for a sustained and pervasive breach of House rules.\n- The Newark by-election for the British House of Commons was held on 5 June 2014 following Patrick Mercer’s resignation.\n- Robert Jenrick of the Conservative Party won the Newark by-election on 5 June 2014 and currently represents Newark.\n- Newark is a UK Parliament constituency in Nottinghamshire, England.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
